      'beginner.week1.r4.action': 'Plant wheat + push Cooking to 2-3 stars',
      'beginner.week1.r4.unlock': 'More shops',
      'beginner.week1.r5.action': 'Harvest first wheat + expand storage',
      'beginner.week1.r5.unlock': 'Storage +50',
      'beginner.week1.r6.action': 'Second hobby ticket → bug-catching',
      'beginner.week1.r6.unlock': '🦋 Bug-catching',
      'beginner.week1.r7.action': 'Stabilize loop + prepare for mid-game',
      'beginner.week1.r7.unlock': 'Co-op building',
      'beginner.week1.note': 'Day 5-7 daily income assumes stable Cooking at 2-3 stars plus wheat production kicking in. Actual income depends on your farming scale and cooking efficiency.',
      'beginner.res.eyebrow': 'Resource management',
      'beginner.res.h2': 'What is worth spending on, and what is not?',
      'beginner.res.intro': 'The game has three core resources: Wishing Stars (scarce), gold (earnable), and time (finite). Each has priorities — spend wisely and you get twice the results for half the effort.',
      'beginner.res.star.h3': '⭐ Wishing Star spending priority',
      'beginner.res.star.t1.h': '🥇 Top priority: bag &amp; storage expansion (first 5 times)',
      'beginner.res.star.t1.p': 'The first 5 bag expansions (+10 slots) and storage expansions (+50 slots) each cost only &lt;strong&gt;10 Wishing Stars&lt;/strong&gt; (normally 25 — a 40% discount). This is the best investment in the game — bag space directly affects gathering and fishing efficiency. Buy them from NPC Ka Ching (across from plot 8 in the northwest suburbs). In total you need &lt;strong&gt;50 stars = +50 bag slots +250 storage slots&lt;/strong&gt;. From the 6th purchase it jumps to 25 stars each, so stop buying after the discount ends.',
      'beginner.res.star.t2.h': '🥈 Second priority: hobby unlocks &amp; Cooking upgrades',
      'beginner.res.star.t2.p': 'Fishing (auto at Lv.2) and Gardening (auto at Lv.3) cost no Wishing Stars. Cooking (Lv.5, via a hobby expansion ticket) is the first real decision — and a must-pick. Later, bug-catching (Lv.8) and bird-watching (Lv.11) each need a ticket. &lt;strong&gt;The higher your Cooking level, the better your high-star odds — the same ingredients earn 50-100% more.&lt;/strong&gt;',
      'beginner.res.star.t3.h': '🥉 Third priority: functional buildings &amp; furniture',
      'beginner.res.star.t3.p': 'Extra stoves (one more stove = 1.3x cooking efficiency), more farmland, and functional storage furniture. These directly boost your earning power — this is "spend money to make money" investing. &lt;strong&gt;One extra stove means 3-5 more dishes a day, roughly +1,000-1,500G/day.&lt;/strong&gt;',
      'beginner.res.star.t4.h': '💡 Emergency uses &amp; places to never spend',
      'beginner.res.star.t4.p': '&lt;strong&gt;Emergency:&lt;/strong&gt; 1 star for a firecracker → sell to Albert Jr. = 1,100G (do not do this often; Wishing Stars are far more precious than gold)&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;❌ Never spend on:&lt;/strong&gt; speeding up crop growth (2 hours is not worth 1 star), buying base ingredients (you get them free from farming/fishing/gathering), pure decoration (consider only after DG Lv.15 advanced building), or speeding up pet/hobby progress',
      'beginner.res.gold.h3': '💰 Gold spending priority',
      'beginner.res.gold.th.priority': 'Priority',
      'beginner.res.gold.th.use': 'Use',
      'beginner.res.gold.th.cost': 'Est. cost',
      'beginner.res.gold.th.return': 'Return',
      'beginner.res.gold.th.note': 'Notes',
