      'money.star.eyebrow': 'Wishing Star economy',
      'money.star.h2': '⭐ The smartest way to spend Wishing Stars',
      'money.star.intro': 'Wishing Stars are the scarcest currency in the game — spending them in the wrong place is costly',
      'money.star.priority.h3': '🏅 Wishing Star spending priority (high to low)',
      'money.star.priority.p1.h': '🥇 Top priority: bag &amp; storage expansion (first 5)',
      'money.star.priority.p1.p': 'The first 5 bag (+10) and storage (+50) expansions cost only &lt;strong&gt;10 Wishing Stars&lt;/strong&gt; each (normally 25). It is the best investment in the game — bag space directly affects production efficiency. From the 6th purchase it jumps to 25 stars and becomes far less worth it.&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style="color:var(--green)"&gt;Advice: buy out the first 5 as soon as possible = 50 stars for +50 bag slots +250 storage slots.&lt;/span&gt;',
      'money.star.priority.p2.h': '🥈 Second priority: hobby unlocks &amp; upgrades',
      'money.star.priority.p2.p': 'The three money-making hobbies — Fishing (Lv.2), Gardening (Lv.3), and Cooking (Lv.5) — must be unlocked first. Leave bug-catching (Lv.5/8/11) and pets (Lv.12/14) for later — they do not directly produce gold.&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style="color:var(--green)"&gt;The higher your Cooking level, the better your odds of high-quality dishes — the same ingredients earn 50-100% more.&lt;/span&gt;',
      'money.star.priority.p3.h': '🥉 Third priority: buildings &amp; decorations (functional)',
      'money.star.priority.p3.p': 'Extra stoves (one more stove = 1.3x cooking efficiency), more fields (higher crop yield), and functional furniture. These directly boost your earning efficiency.&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style="color:var(--green)"&gt;Decorative furniture is the lowest priority — pretty, but it produces no gold.&lt;/span&gt;',
      'money.star.priority.p4.h': '💡 Quick-cash trick: Wishing Star → firecracker → 1100G',
      'money.star.priority.p4.p': 'Buy a firecracker with 1 Wishing Star → sell it to Albert Jr. = &lt;strong&gt;1,100 gold&lt;/strong&gt;. A quick way to cash out when you need money — but in the long run, Wishing Stars are far more precious than gold, so &lt;strong&gt;do not do this often&lt;/strong&gt;.',
      'money.star.priority.p5.h': '⚠️ Never spend Wishing Stars on these',
      'money.star.priority.p5.p': '❌ Speeding up crop growth (waiting 2h is not worth 1 star)&amp;nbsp; ❌ Buying base ingredients (grow/fish/gather them free)&amp;nbsp; ❌ Pure decoration (only buy later with spare stars)',
      'money.star.roi.h3': '📊 Wishing Star spending ROI comparison',
      'money.star.roi.th.use': 'Use',
