      'prog.hobbies.order.heading': '🏅 Optimal Unlock Order &amp; Decision Logic',
      'prog.hobbies.order.th.order': 'Order',
      'prog.hobbies.order.th.hobby': 'Hobby',
      'prog.hobbies.order.th.reason': 'Why Choose It',
      'prog.hobbies.order.th.wrong': 'What if you pick wrong?',
      'prog.hobbies.order.o1.hobby': '🎣 Fishing',
      'prog.hobbies.order.o1.reason': 'Auto-unlocks, no choice. Provides a steady source of fish — the base of every cooking recipe.',
      'prog.hobbies.order.o1.wrong': '—— (auto-unlocks, can\'t be missed)',
      'prog.hobbies.order.o2.hobby': '🌱 Gardening',
      'prog.hobbies.order.o2.reason': 'Auto-unlocks, no choice. Farming is the other half of the ingredient base — fish + crops = the recipe system.',
      'prog.hobbies.order.o2.wrong': '—— (auto-unlocks, can\'t be missed)',
      'prog.hobbies.order.o3.hobby': '🍳 &lt;strong&gt;Cooking ⬅ Top pick!&lt;/strong&gt;',
      'prog.hobbies.order.o3.reason': '&lt;strong&gt;The only hobby that builds a positive money loop.&lt;/strong&gt; Fishing and farming output → cooked into dishes → sold for ×2-7. Skip Cooking and you\'ll only be able to sell raw materials early on, capping daily income around 2,000-3,000G; pick it and 5,000-8,000G/day comes easily.&lt;br&gt;Bug catching and birdwatching are pure expenses — they take time but produce no gold. Come back to them once you\'re rich, and they\'ll be far more efficient.',
      'prog.hobbies.order.o3.wrong': '&lt;strong&gt;Picking bug catching/birdwatching = the "three poor years" route.&lt;/strong&gt; Gold is extremely tight early on — buying seeds, expanding, and upgrading all become a struggle. DG leveling also slows because you can\'t afford the tasks that cost gold. The good news: Lv.8 lets you recover — but you\'ll be 3 levels behind.',
      'prog.hobbies.order.o4.hobby': '🦋 &lt;strong&gt;Bug Catching&lt;/strong&gt;',
      'prog.hobbies.order.o4.reason': 'For the second ticket, recommend bug catching. Reasons: ① insect lures let you farm in one spot — drop an inflatable lure and it keeps attracting bugs, unlike birdwatching\'s map-wide searching; ② insects are a major home-score source, and high-star specimens = big score; ③ the bug shop has useful items (including the puzzle dream, used to level Dream after Lv.16).',
      'prog.hobbies.order.o4.wrong': 'Birdwatching isn\'t bad either, but it levels less efficiently (searching the whole map for birds). It won\'t ruin your game — Lv.11 lets you catch up.',
      'prog.hobbies.order.o5.hobby': '🔭 &lt;strong&gt;Birdwatching&lt;/strong&gt;',
      'prog.hobbies.order.o5.reason': '&lt;strong&gt;Last one to round out. Birdwatching\'s biggest edge is that photographing the same bird repeatedly still builds level progress&lt;/strong&gt; — no need to hunt for new species. That means you can camp one fixed spot and level in peace. Once done, all five production/collection hobbies are unlocked.',
      'prog.hobbies.order.o5.wrong': '—— (third ticket; only birdwatching is left to pick)',
      'prog.hobbies.order.o6.hobby': '🐱 &lt;strong&gt;Cat Keeping&lt;/strong&gt;',
      'prog.hobbies.order.o6.reason': 'The gateway to the pet system. The basic cat-care tutorial must be finished — it\'s a hard prerequisite for dogs. Daily cat care is simpler, a good intro to the pet system.',
      'prog.hobbies.order.o6.wrong': '—— (only unlockable at Lv.12, can\'t pick it early by mistake)',
      'prog.hobbies.order.o7.hobby': '🐕 &lt;strong&gt;Dog Keeping&lt;/strong&gt;',
      'prog.hobbies.order.o7.reason': 'Unlocks after finishing basic cat care. Cats and dogs can be kept together for a complete pet system. Dogs need more interaction (walking etc.) but reward you more richly.',
      'prog.hobbies.order.o7.wrong': '—— (requires finishing basic cat care — a hard prerequisite)',
      'prog.hobbies.tips.heading': '📈 Leveling Tips for Each Hobby',
      'prog.hobbies.tips.fishing.heading': '🎣 Fishing Leveling',
      'prog.hobbies.tips.fishing.body': '• Prioritize high-value spots: ocean (summer) &gt; river &gt; pond&lt;br&gt;• Sea-fishing event week is the best time to power-level&lt;br&gt;• Match the spot to the weather: sunny = sea fishing, rainy = river fishing&lt;br&gt;• &lt;strong&gt;Higher fishing level → higher star-fish rate → higher sale price&lt;/strong&gt;',
      'prog.hobbies.tips.gardening.heading': '🌱 Gardening Leveling',
      'prog.hobbies.tips.gardening.body': '• Rotate fast crops (potato 2h) → frequent harvests = frequent XP&lt;br&gt;• Never leave fields empty — replant as soon as you harvest&lt;br&gt;• High-quality flowers (rose, lily) add extra home score&lt;br&gt;• &lt;strong&gt;Gardening level affects crop star rating and yield&lt;/strong&gt;',
      'prog.hobbies.tips.cooking.heading': '🍳 Cooking Leveling',
      'prog.hobbies.tips.cooking.body': '• &lt;strong&gt;Four-stove cooking&lt;/strong&gt;: arrange 4 stoves in a square, stand in the middle to manage 4 dishes at once&lt;br&gt;• Batch-cook the same dish for max efficiency&lt;br&gt;• Prioritize high-value recipes: blueberry jam, fish &amp; chips, fried carp&lt;br&gt;• Cooking level = higher star rate ↑ = higher price ↑ = more money ↑',
      'prog.hobbies.tips.bug.heading': '🦋 Bug Catching Leveling',
      'prog.hobbies.tips.bug.body': '• Use inflatable lures to farm bugs in one spot (place in bug-dense areas)&lt;br&gt;• Different seasons/weather bring different bugs&lt;br&gt;• High-star specimens count toward home score&lt;br&gt;• The bug shop sells the puzzle dream (used to level Dream after Lv.16)',
      'prog.hobbies.tips.bird.heading': '🔭 Birdwatching Leveling',
      'prog.hobbies.tips.bird.body': '• &lt;strong&gt;Photographing the same bird repeatedly still builds progress&lt;/strong&gt; — no need to chase new species&lt;br&gt;• Find a fixed bird spot and level in peace&lt;br&gt;• Bird activity varies by time (most species at dawn and dusk)&lt;br&gt;• Special weather (rainbow days) sharply boosts rare-bird spawn rate',
      'prog.hobbies.tips.pets.heading': '🐱🐕 Pet Leveling',
      'prog.hobbies.tips.pets.body': '• Daily interaction (feeding, petting, playing) builds affection&lt;br&gt;• Finish the basic cat-care tutorial before you can unlock dogs&lt;br&gt;• Cats and dogs can coexist — the two pets\' affection is tracked independently&lt;br&gt;• Higher affection → new interactions → home-score bonus',
      'prog.hobbies.npc.heading': '📍 Key NPC Locations Quick Reference',
